From f50d06c6120ad761a6edba0d8b07e3f4e4e09700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:04:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): offer kind='assignment' only where a
 different profile can take the card

On single-profile hosts (no kanban.orchestrator_profile, creator == assignee) kind='assignment'
always fails with no_capable_supervisor, yet the agent_owned_block refusal, the kanban_block
schema, the worker prompt and the awaiting remedy all prescribed it: 38 cards in 72 h hit the
wall, and some turned into asks to David for agent work or producer-less self-parks.

- kanban_assignment_routing.supervisor_available(task): _supervisor(task)[0] is not None.
- block_policy_error offers assignment only with task=(conn, id) and an available supervisor;
  otherwise it lists the one-profile routes (owner card + card park, needs=[...],
  kanban_supervisor_request). Tool and CLI pass task= per card.
- route()'s no_capable_supervisor refusal names those routes instead of a config change.
- Schema, KANBAN_GUIDANCE and the agent_action_wait remedy qualify assignment.
Routing behavior and config defaults are unchanged.
